  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math> are the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></math> is equal to ________.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>iv</mi></mfenced></math><br />from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>iv</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>vi</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>vi</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br />from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math><br />So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p>"
  }
